HONEST LIMITS (recorded, not hidden)
------------------------------------
1. rtl/ternary_mac_demo_top.xdc targets the QMTech Wukong V1 (XC7A100T-FGG676,
   LEDs R23/T23). The _200t.bit was placed on an xc7a200tfbg676 chipdb (die
   level) and loads on the AX7203 (FBG484) because the design touches no pin
   the die cannot resolve - but its two OBUFs drive pins the AX7203 routes
   ELSEWHERE (AX7203 LEDs are B13/C13, see evidence/ax7203_build). The shipped
   demo therefore never showed visible behaviour on the AX7203. This matches
   the v2 header's own defect list and the withdrawn-performance history.
2. The design's clock is a 20-stage LUT1 ring oscillator
   (ALLOW_COMBINATORIAL_LOOPS): uncharacterised, and probe-verified NOT to
   oscillate (evidence/clock_probe/shipped_bitstream_analysis.log: all 6 FDRE
   clocked by net 'osc', the dead one). The shipped bitstream proves toolchain
   loadability, NOT datapath behaviour. Functional smoke stays issue #5 [R5].
3. Byte-identical .bit regeneration was NOT attempted: nextpnr-xilinx and
   xc7frames2bit are not installed on this host. Structural equivalence is the
   proven level; a byte-level re-cut requires the openXC7 flow (future work).

